{"code": 0, "output": "Server Redundancy\n\nIn the new redundancy scheme, the second server operates in a “hot standby” mode. It receives copies of records but does not respond to user requests while the primary server is functional. The term “hot standby” is not related to the temperature of the hardware. It means that the backup server is ready to quickly take over the workload without a full reinitialization of data.\n\nDuring testing, the primary server was disconnected from the power supply for 90 seconds. The backup server began responding within four seconds, and some clients automatically resent their requests. Two identical requests should not result in two identical purchases. Therefore, each order is assigned a permanent key, which is retained when the request is resent. The key is used to identify the order, not to encrypt its contents.", "seconds": 8.178272624994861, "first_token_seconds": 0.875324041, "prompt_tokens": 201, "type": "result", "label": "Q4_K_M-control", "id": "technical-standby", "pass_number": 1, "warmup": false, "thermal_wait_seconds": 0, "memory_before": {"footprint": 350147624, "resident": 5863374848, "resident_process_peak": 5969379328, "thermal": 0, "metal_allocated": 5874761728}, "memory_after": {"footprint": 357798952, "resident": 5839224832, "resident_process_peak": 5969379328, "thermal": 0, "metal_allocated": 5874761728}, "memory_peak": {"footprint": 358241320, "resident": 5874696192, "resident_process_peak": 5969379328, "thermal": 0, "metal_allocated": 5875761152}, "memory_samples": 79, "system": {"swap": "vm.swapusage: total = 2048.00M  used = 1062.38M  free = 985.62M  (encrypted)", "thermal": 0}, "output_retokenized_count": 162}
{"code": 0, "output": "Delivery Plan\n\nThe supplier has prepared three shipments of parts for the assembly workshop. The first shipment consists of 480 casings, the second of 960 covers, and the third contains spare seals. The presence of parts in the warehouse does not yet mean that the cargo has been handed over to the carrier. A signed delivery note confirms the shipment; an automatic order creation notification is not considered such confirmation.\n\nThe dispatcher reported that the truck will arrive on Tuesday between nine and eleven o’clock. However, the warehouse worker will only be able to accept the cargo after ten. Therefore, the driver must first deliver the covers to a neighboring warehouse and then bring the casings to the workshop. There is no need to change the addresses on the delivery notes: only the order of stops is changing, not the recipients. If the first stop is delayed, the driver must call the dispatcher.", "seconds": 8.830134082993027, "first_token_seconds": 0.89180925, "prompt_tokens": 220, "type": "result", "label": "Q4_K_M-control", "id": "technical-logistics", "pass_number": 1, "warmup": false, "thermal_wait_seconds": 0, "memory_before": {"footprint": 357815336, "resident": 5846958080, "resident_process_peak": 5969379328, "thermal": 0, "metal_allocated": 5874761728}, "memory_after": {"footprint": 358208552, "resident": 5855789056, "resident_process_peak": 5969379328, "thermal": 0, "metal_allocated": 5874761728}, "memory_peak": {"footprint": 358290472, "resident": 5857984512, "resident_process_peak": 5969379328, "thermal": 0, "metal_allocated": 5875761152}, "memory_samples": 86, "system": {"swap": "vm.swapusage: total = 2048.00M  used = 1062.38M  free = 985.62M  (encrypted)", "thermal": 0}, "output_retokenized_count": 182}
