{"code": 0, "output": "Cooling Test\n\nA closed-loop cooling system for a laser machine was tested on the test bench. The pump circulated water through a filter and a heat exchanger, after which it returned to the reservoir. At a flow rate of 18 liters per minute, the outlet temperature remained at 27 degrees. This is the result of a laboratory test, not a guarantee of the same temperature under any load. The operator recorded readings every five minutes and did not change any settings during the test series.\n\nAfter replacing the filter, the pressure before the heat exchanger decreased, but the flow rate remained unchanged. Engineer Anna hypothesized that some of the water was bypassing through a bypass valve. She asked the technician to close it only for the duration of the measurements. The technician complied but then returned the valve to its original position: it was prohibited to leave it closed when the pump was stopped. No signs of leaks at the connections were found.", "seconds": 10.181429000018397, "first_token_seconds": 1.06540675, "prompt_tokens": 237, "type": "result", "label": "Q4_K_M-control", "id": "technical-cooling", "pass_number": 1, "warmup": false, "thermal_wait_seconds": 0, "memory_before": {"footprint": 358568976, "resident": 5822152704, "resident_process_peak": 5969379328, "thermal": 0, "metal_allocated": 5874761728}, "memory_after": {"footprint": 358618128, "resident": 5832785920, "resident_process_peak": 5969379328, "thermal": 0, "metal_allocated": 5874761728}, "memory_peak": {"footprint": 358749200, "resident": 5832818688, "resident_process_peak": 5969379328, "thermal": 0, "metal_allocated": 5875761152}, "memory_samples": 97, "system": {"swap": "vm.swapusage: total = 2048.00M  used = 1062.38M  free = 985.62M  (encrypted)", "thermal": 0}, "output_retokenized_count": 191}
