{"code": 0, "output": "Service Update\n\nThe service accepts report generation requests and places them in a queue. Short requests are processed immediately, while larger reports are handled by a background process. The cache stores the completed result for only ten minutes. If a user resubmits the same request within this period, the server returns the cached response. This does not mean that the new request is discarded: a separate entry remains in the log, indicating the source of the result.\n\nAfter the update, a bug was discovered: canceled requests sometimes remained in the queue and were executed later. Programmer Oleg initially suggested clearing the entire queue upon cancellation, but a colleague explained that this would result in the loss of other users' tasks. They decided to delete only the entry with the matching identifier. Canceling one report should not alter the state of other reports or clear their cached results.", "seconds": 9.089486750017386, "first_token_seconds": 0.966839209, "prompt_tokens": 224, "type": "result", "label": "Q4_K_M-control", "id": "technical-software", "pass_number": 1, "warmup": false, "thermal_wait_seconds": 0, "memory_before": {"footprint": 358618128, "resident": 5834113024, "resident_process_peak": 5969379328, "thermal": 0, "metal_allocated": 5874761728}, "memory_after": {"footprint": 358634512, "resident": 5833129984, "resident_process_peak": 5969379328, "thermal": 0, "metal_allocated": 5874761728}, "memory_peak": {"footprint": 358716432, "resident": 5836521472, "resident_process_peak": 5969379328, "thermal": 0, "metal_allocated": 5875761152}, "memory_samples": 87, "system": {"swap": "vm.swapusage: total = 2048.00M  used = 1062.38M  free = 985.62M  (encrypted)", "thermal": 0}, "output_retokenized_count": 170}
